From bde79c26da788d1affe56848574dc4b6d3e4ac08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:44:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] filecache: a player waits out a source that stops before the
 end of the file

When the network source of a cached file stops sending (a Wi-Fi that drops,
a streaming service that stalls), CFileCache::Read() waits 10 s for data
and then returns 0. CDVDInputStreamFile takes 0 for the end of the file,
the demuxer for AVERROR_EOF, and the player ends the video as if it had
been played to its end, with whatever an add-on does at an end (marked as
watched, the next episode). The cache thread meanwhile gives a source that
stopped up after 4 reopenings (7.5 s) and ends the input, which is the end
of the file as well. A file of known length whose bytes are still missing
has not ended: its source has stalled.

A reader that can stop its reads at once (IOControl::READ_ABORT) and gives
IOControl::READ_WAIT around its reads (a player, which buffers meanwhile)
now waits for such a source instead:

- CFileCache::Read() waits, in slices of 100 ms between which the reader's
  function is called with how long it has waited, until there is data,
  the input ends, a seek fails, or the reader aborts.
- The cache thread keeps reopening the source at the byte it stopped at,
  every 4 s after the first pauses, for as long as it stays silent, and
  gives it up after 5 minutes without data, or at once when the server
  answers the range with a 4xx that will not change (an expired or removed
  link). The read that then finds nothing fails (-1, IOControl::
  SOURCE_FAILED answers 1): it is not the end of the file. A 416 (the file
  is shorter than it said) and a source that cannot seek (a server without
  ranges) end the file as before.
- A stall logs its first reopenings, then a line every 30 s, and a line
  when the source sends again.

Readers that do not ask (thumbnails, stream details, scans), sources of
unknown length (live streams) and the end of a file are as before: no
data for 10 s is the end, 4 reopenings, and the end of the file at once.

Host test of CFileCache (FileCache.cpp and CircularCache.cpp of the tree,
with a source that holds, drops and refuses like an HTTP source), 32
checks: before, 17 fail (a 12 s hold ends the file at 10 s with 1 of 8 MiB
read; a 10 s outage ends it after 4 reopenings; a source that never comes
back, one that refuses the file, and a stop all read as the end of the
file); after, all pass with ASan+UBSan and TSan, and the 18 checks of the
abort change still pass.
